server: give the chat parameters the defaults of common_params
Fold-into: upstream/jinja

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

struct server_chat_params (tools/server/server-common.h) has no default for
use_jinja, prefill_assistant, reasoning_format, allow_image, allow_audio and
allow_video. The server sets each field, but a caller that sets only some of
them reads an indeterminate value: test-chat sets use_jinja,
enable_thinking, reasoning_budget and reasoning_format, and
oaicompat_chat_params_parse then reads opt.prefill_assistant
(server-common.cpp). MemorySanitizer reports a use of an uninitialized value
there.

The change: the defaults of common_params (use_jinja true,
prefill_assistant true, reasoning_format DEEPSEEK) and false for the three
media flags. The server sets each field, thus its behavior does not change.

diff --git a/tools/server/server-common.h b/tools/server/server-common.h
index 9894f5f..2a63d5f 100644
--- a/tools/server/server-common.h
+++ b/tools/server/server-common.h
@@ -306,14 +306,15 @@ std::vector<server_tokens> tokenize_input_prompts(
 
 // global server parameters for chat formatting / parsing
 struct server_chat_params {
-    bool use_jinja;
-    bool prefill_assistant;
-    common_reasoning_format reasoning_format;
+    // the defaults of common_params: a caller that sets only some fields reads no indeterminate value
+    bool use_jinja = true;
+    bool prefill_assistant = true;
+    common_reasoning_format reasoning_format = COMMON_REASONING_FORMAT_DEEPSEEK;
     std::map<std::string, std::string> chat_template_kwargs; // mapping key --> json value
     common_chat_templates_ptr tmpls;
-    bool allow_image;
-    bool allow_audio;
-    bool allow_video;
+    bool allow_image = false;
+    bool allow_audio = false;
+    bool allow_video = false;
     bool enable_thinking = true;
     int  reasoning_budget = -1;
     std::string reasoning_budget_message;
